+
+Actual native correction qualification must bind both observed stage responses to the
+same worker/context, require failed fresh-check provenance before correction, and permit
+at most one correction. New checks bind the correction candidate; correcting a synthetic
+oracle cannot fill missing native XML or accept engineering scope. Restarted operator
+processes must preserve exclusive receipts, application/collection order and interrupted
+stop markers. Explicit stop-marker injection is distinct from a crash during application
+and from native Fabro checkpoint resume. Every refusal remains part of offline reporting.
+
+Fresh paired admission drafts must retain public-source/provider freshness, exact native
+check proposals and unresolved applicability/roles. An accepted prior patch or budget
+exception cannot fill missing native decisions. Bind an offline decision to the exact
+reviewed matrix before executable worker/stage/meter instruction preparation.
+
+Both arms may share reversible serialization normalization: retain original source
+bytes/hashes and full contracts, preserve all ordered JSON values and every validation
+constraint, and transmit a full context digest instead of duplicate bookkeeping. Retain
+initial oversized attempts. Reconstructed native-wrapper sizes are not actual transmitted
+payloads or provider token usage; require observed preflight and unchanged request guards.
+Official model alias documentation is not effective runtime observation or permission
+to accept previously unrecognized response models.
+
+Optional request_parameters must be selected explicitly in a SHA-bound private Flash
+instruction, not inferred from task class or installed skills. Accept only the complete
+non-thinking JSON profile: thinking.type=disabled, reasoning_effort=none and
+response_format.type=json_object. Partial/expanded controls and other providers/models
+are refused. Instructions without the field keep existing behavior. Preserve source
+messages, model/output limits, stream and tool-selection constraints. Added projection
+bytes count before reservation; the raw request ceiling still applies before projection.
+
+Actual native payload captures, local projection and effective upstream transmission
+are separate evidence. Preserve original wrappers/parameters; successful report/exit
+after a deliberate local refusal supplies no candidate, provider usage or engineering
+acceptance. Qualify every dynamic stage envelope; implementation headroom does not
+prove correction/review fit. Native offline scope/role/QNX inputs remain mandatory.
+
+Dynamic correction/review envelope drafts must independently bind exact worker bytes,
+candidate/application identity, complete source inventory, check-file SHA/status and
+feedback/current-source hashes. Correction requires a failed current candidate/check
+binding; review must preserve failed/missing/skipped states. Historical synthetic
+inputs qualify protocol only and cannot satisfy current real-trial freshness.
+
+Measure whole stage payloads, including native wrapper/tool projection and candidate
+content. Implementation preflight does not prove dynamic-stage fit. Oversize envelopes
+export refusal evidence and terminate; complete artifacts, checks and limits remain.
+Local capture guards are distinct from production meter reservation and engineering
+admission. Bounded source retrieval requires its own actual native delivery, per-result
+and aggregate accounting before live use.
+
+### Stage source snapshots (US29)
+
+`optimization serve --stage correction|review --stage-manifest PATH
+--stage-manifest-sha256 SHA256` selects a pinned stage_retrieval_manifest. This mode
+cannot combine --sources and advertises only get_source_excerpt. Required artifacts
+(binding/candidate/checks/feedback) and original/candidate file references contain
+path, sha256 and bytes. Candidate files exactly cover the worker write set; original
+files match its baseline inventory. All are revalidated before delivery. Excerpts
+carry manifest/stage/candidate/check/feedback pins and raw source hashes. Changed
+snapshots require a new stage/budget; sealed records create no authority. Existing
+250-line, 3,000-byte excerpt, escaped 5,000-byte result and 12,000-byte aggregate
+bounds apply. Provider RequestMeter independently limits every complete message
+history and total stage requests/input/output. Offline reports retain native missing
+or failed evidence and engineering acceptance pending.
+
+
+### Complete tool exchange and final candidate capture (US30)
+
+A stage with multiple observed replies must preserve every observed request/response,
+usage and instruction pin. All prior replies must end in complete bounded tool calls;
+an earlier complete candidate or an incomplete tool turn makes final selection invalid.
+The following request must contain the unchanged previous message prefix, the exact
+completed assistant tool calls and one exact sealed source result per call identifier.
+Only instruction-selected get_source_excerpt calls may participate. Resolve the view
+within the bound workspace and validate its complete source/check/feedback manifest
+against the live protected worker binding, current candidate and latest check SHA.
+
+Capture only the final complete structured reply. Unknown/reserved usage, conflicting
+records, substituted conversation/results, stale worker/source/check bindings and
+truncated final output refuse before candidate application. Direct application validates
+the same witness chain. Exclusive receipts, one-correction scope and interrupted/replay
+protection still apply. Fresh post-correction collection binds the new candidate and
+source inventory; an advisory review uses the exact new feedback and cannot accept
+engineering decisions. Keep command records complete outside conversation; concise
+artifact references in native command output may remove duplicated bookkeeping.
+Synthetic usage/counts do not measure live full-candidate output-token feasibility.
+
+The pinned native codec may omit null assistant content in a tool-only turn; allow
+only this exact absent/null equivalence. Other message/result substitutions refuse.
+A direct receipt cannot select an earlier complete reply when a later stage ticket
+exists. Namespace each fresh collector directory by its full worker binding SHA so
+same-arm repetitions retain separate immutable measurements. Native continuation
+following a length-truncated reply remains subject to the same full-request guard;
+a stopped meter refuses capture even when the incomplete reply has known usage.
+
+
+### Offline admission review subjects (US31)
+
+Review byte pins establish provenance only. Verify exact proposed check/profile/label
+identities and genuine native ID/status fields without treating unchanged exports as
+closed source impact. Keep discovered checks, historical execution and newly collected
+results separate. Native scope/role/independence decisions require their own subject-bound
+human record; prior local patch approval and model/budget authority do not fill them.
+
+A decision template may prefill exact subject hashes while remaining unreviewed and
+unaccepted. Drafting preferences are distinct from applicability acceptance. Copy a
+sealed template into a separate decision record before entering a human decision;
+never edit the sealed evidence packet. Known-path QNX metadata checks establish neither
+archive authenticity nor license eligibility. Native request/candidate qualification
+with synthetic bytes creates no real trial instruction, native acceptance or savings.
+
+
+US32 Linux dependency measurements preserve the pinned source and public dependency
+identities and explicit QNX skip. Network isolation and native fetch guards are
+operational probe controls, not native applicability waivers. Loading/analysis/cache
+results cannot satisfy compilation, execution or human acceptance. No substitute SDK,
+unverified checksum, automatic scope acceptance or new live-stage instruction is produced.
+
+
+US33 metadata mirrors serve exact captured public index bytes bound to URL/digest,
+never invented package or SDK content. Explicit downloader controls and network
+isolation constrain probes without silently changing native applicability. Missing
+metadata, denied downloads and cache drift remain failures. No source/lockfile,
+checksum, live instruction, trusted review decision or publication is synthesized.
+
+US34 preserves complete prepared metadata as an immutable native input and distinguishes
+metadata delivery, repository availability, archive integrity and extraction. A native
+cache hit followed by filename rejection remains failed extraction. A configured archive
+route without an observed request or successful extraction remains unqualified. Exact
+registry source declarations bound by native lock hashes may identify missing public
+archive/patch inputs; their existence does not establish acquired bytes or dependency
+closure. QNX skip/download denial and offline acceptance boundaries remain unchanged.
+
+US35 binds exact public module source/archive/patch inputs to unchanged native registry
+and lock identities. Captured input manifests are immutable per probe. Byte delivery,
+integrity, completed repository markers, package loading and configured analysis are
+distinct predicates. Incomplete extraction remains explicit despite successful HTTP.
+A direct target query accepts no configured/native verification scope. Additional testing
+dependency pins require their actual source bindings; missing inputs and exhausted
+stages export reports and terminate with engineering decisions pending offline.
+
+US36 binds Bats source dependencies through the original native module archive and
+checksum declarations. Existing release-checksum metadata may bind future tool inputs
+only through exact original extension attributes. Cached binary existence and matching
+checksums supply neither current input admission nor execution/engineering acceptance.
+Mirrors must distinguish attempted status/bytes from completed response writes; retain
+old unknown delivery and runtime mismatch records. Corrected Python/tool bindings and
+completed native repository markers remain separate from configured analysis/build/tests.
+
+US37 binds cached Linux Buf executables through the original native extension attributes,
+checksum-list bytes and wrapper/module source. Cache import, completed HTTP writes, native
+repository markers/executable hashes and actual execution remain separate measurements.
+An observed compiler archive outside the declared input scope stops the bounded stage;
+missing cache payloads/sizes/licenses do not become accepted compiler readiness. Native
+source/locks stay unchanged, QNX is skipped and engineering review occurs offline.
+
+US38 treats release-reported size/digest, acquired payload SHA-256, archive inventories/
+notices, completed transport, native materialization and configured analysis as separate
+predicates. A remounted volume receives fresh read-only input bindings; old workspace
+records stay unchanged and no queue is resumed or migrated. Linux compiler acquisition
+uses an explicit new bounded stage, not unused US37 attempts or zero-byte missing-input
+subtotals. Payload notices never establish accepted licensing/tool qualification.
+Unlisted dependencies/QNX remain denied; native scope and engineering acceptance stay
+pending offline even if analysis passes.
+
+US39 retains a missing release-asset digest as null and verifies the acquired Linux
+Coreutils payload with the checksum bound to original native registry/module/wrapper
+bytes. Source-license and actual payload-notice measurements stay separate. Only the
+one selected public archive enters a fresh finite allowlist; native source/locks,
+historical storage/queues, QNX skip and offline engineering acceptance are unchanged.
+Transport, executable hash/mode, repository markers and configured analysis remain
+separate predicates; unlisted inputs stop the stage before scope widening.
+
+US40 extends the fresh exact-input allowlist only to the pinned Linux GCC package.
+Release metadata/digest, acquired hash, actual payload notices, repository loading and
+configured analysis are separate predicates. The inherited native QNX license-path
+attribute is source metadata; do not read that path or infer QNX applicability. An
+unconfigured package query measures native cache extraction before configured analysis.
+Unlisted dependencies stop this stage; successful loading never accepts qualification.
+
+US41 verifies standalone Linux jq bytes against original native SHA-384 integrity.
+A separately measured SHA-256 supports exact mirror/cache delivery without inventing
+native SHA-256 authority. ELF/static strings/source-license findings do not establish
+execution compatibility, complete linked-component licensing or accepted qualification.
+Only the selected binary enters the fresh allowlist; unlisted dependencies stop analysis.
+Native repository loading and configured analysis remain separate measured predicates.
+
+US42 preserves BSD tar historical native URL/checksum and canonical release URL as
+separate provenance fields. Original SHA-256 verifies acquired bytes; builder/source
+licenses and static binary findings do not establish complete component licensing,
+execution compatibility or qualification. Exact repository loading precedes configured
+analysis; unlisted inputs stop the finite stage without source/lock edits or acceptance.
+
+US43 preserves zstd historical native URL/checksum and canonical release URL as
+separate provenance fields. Original SHA-256 verifies acquired bytes; builder/source
+licenses and static binary findings do not establish complete component licensing,
+execution compatibility or qualification. Exact repository loading precedes configured
+analysis; unlisted inputs stop the finite stage without source/lock edits or acceptance.
+
+US44 binds OCI objects through the original native image-index digest and exact
+linux/amd64 descriptor/config/layer closure, including bounded uncompressed diff-ID
+validation. Anonymous acquisition tokens exist in memory only, without SSD/log storage.
+Native probes use original-source-supported OCI_GET_TOKEN_ALLOW_FAIL after preserving
+local token denial; exact cached/mirrored public objects do not qualify live native
+registry authentication. No fabricated token, tag substitution, native source/lock edit,
+image/container execution, build/test or engineering acceptance follows.
